{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-39945","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63582","text":"Slice B, Commit 3 — the "},{"id":"spn-63583","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63584","text":" surface: closure memo"}]},{"id":"blk-39946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63585","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-63586","text":" CLOSED. "},{"id":"spn-63587","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run48"},{"id":"spn-63588","text":" PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (6s, 71 rows). "},{"id":"spn-63589","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate48"},{"id":"spn-63590","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63591","marks":["bold"],"text":"19/19 ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"spn-63592","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-63593","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep"},{"id":"spn-63594","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63595","marks":["bold"],"text":"16/16 green"},{"id":"spn-63596","text":" (141s, reference + native), L-0 tier unmoved."}]},{"id":"blk-39947","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63597","text":"Commit 2 gave a route a canonical form and an identity but no spelling. Commit 3 gives it the ruled spelling in both directions:"}]},{"id":"blk-39948","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7)"},{"id":"blk-39949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63598","text":"and closes the two things that spelling makes reachable — the Q4 writer-15 reservation, and a silent world substitution in the authoring draft."}]},{"id":"blk-39950","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63599","text":"1. What shipped"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-39952","spans":[{"id":"spn-63600","text":"file"}]},{"id":"blk-39953","spans":[{"id":"spn-63601","text":"change"}]}],"id":"blk-39951","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-39954","spans":[{"id":"spn-63602","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39955","spans":[{"id":"spn-63603","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_RE"},{"id":"spn-63604","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63605","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROUTE_KEYS"},{"id":"spn-63606","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63607","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-63608","text":", the route branch in "},{"id":"spn-63609","marks":["code"],"text":"_parse_core_permissive"},{"id":"spn-63610","text":"; bootstrap "},{"id":"spn-63611","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63612","text":" message split off from "},{"id":"spn-63613","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-63614","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63615","marks":["code"],"text":"=="}]}],[{"id":"blk-39956","spans":[{"id":"spn-63616","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39957","spans":[{"id":"spn-63617","text":"route section emitted after the edges, "},{"id":"spn-63618","marks":["code"],"text":"_emit_body"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39958","spans":[{"id":"spn-63619","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_canonical.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39959","spans":[{"id":"spn-63620","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_ROUTE_WRITER_RESERVED"},{"id":"spn-63621","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63622","marks":["code"],"text":"routes_of_artifact"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39960","spans":[{"id":"spn-63623","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39961","spans":[{"id":"spn-63624","marks":["code"],"text":"check_route_writer_reservation"},{"id":"spn-63625","text":", "},{"id":"spn-63626","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39962","spans":[{"id":"spn-63627","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_draft.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39963","spans":[{"id":"spn-63628","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-63629","text":", the computed "},{"id":"spn-63630","marks":["code"],"text":"_draft_loss"},{"id":"spn-63631","text":" round-trip, both draft doors"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39964","spans":[{"id":"spn-63632","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39965","spans":[{"id":"spn-63633","text":"call site widened to the composed door"}]}],[{"id":"blk-39966","spans":[{"id":"spn-63634","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run47.py"}]},{"id":"blk-39967","spans":[{"id":"spn-63635","text":"closing NOTE corrected (it said \"there is no "},{"id":"spn-63636","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63637","text":" surface\")"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-39968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63638","text":"The parser's job stops at "},{"id":"spn-63639","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"this line says a route.\""},{"id":"spn-63640","text":" Endpoint roles, the one-shot source law, the body range, duplicates and the budget are all the seal's, and they are the seal's for a route arriving from "},{"id":"spn-63641","marks":["bold"],"text":"any"},{"id":"spn-63642","text":" surface. Every Q7 row proves this twice: the parse "},{"id":"spn-63643","marks":["bold"],"text":"succeeds"},{"id":"spn-63644","text":" and the seal "},{"id":"spn-63645","marks":["bold"],"text":"refuses"},{"id":"spn-63646","text":". A parser that had helpfully re-implemented one of these fails the first half."}]},{"id":"blk-39969","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63647","text":"2. Five autonomous decisions — please confirm or overrule"}]},{"id":"blk-39970","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63648","text":"(a) The draft "},{"id":"spn-63649","marks":["bold"],"text":"REFUSES"},{"id":"spn-63650","text":" route-bearing worlds rather than being widened"}]},{"id":"blk-39971","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63651","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-63652","marks":["code"],"text":"WorldDraft"},{"id":"spn-63653","text":" stores a world as "},{"id":"spn-63654","marks":["code"],"text":"(objects, edges)"},{"id":"spn-63655","text":". A route is neither, so it was invisible. "},{"id":"spn-63656","marks":["bold"],"text":"Measured before the guard was written:"},{"id":"spn-63657","text":" opening the one-route world for editing produced no error and yielded "},{"id":"spn-63658","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d3e555be…"},{"id":"spn-63659","text":" — the route-free twin, a perfectly good world with a perfectly good id. Legal, which is what makes it dangerous."}]},{"id":"blk-39972","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63660","text":"Widening the draft to carry routes is not a language change: it is a new revision of "},{"id":"spn-63661","marks":["bold"],"text":"every persisted authoring document"},{"id":"spn-63662","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-63663","marks":["code"],"text":"ForgeProjectV2"},{"id":"spn-63664","text":", the v0.6-0 recovery journal, the draft-state ledger, the canvas reconciler. That is a document-format migration and it does not belong inside a language slice, so commit 3 ships a "},{"id":"spn-63665","marks":["bold"],"text":"refusal"},{"id":"spn-63666","text":" and defers the widening."}]},{"id":"blk-39973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63667","text":"The guard is a "},{"id":"spn-63668","marks":["bold"],"text":"computed round-trip"},{"id":"spn-63669","text":", not a construct blacklist:"}]},{"id":"blk-39974","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"want = W.lower_graph(g).semantic_artifact_id\ngot, err = _seal(objects, edges, profile)\nif err is None and got == want: return None      # nothing was lost"},{"id":"blk-39975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63670","text":"It names no construct, so it will refuse the "},{"id":"spn-63671","marks":["italic"],"text":"next"},{"id":"spn-63672","text":" unrepresentable construct without being edited — the same property that made "},{"id":"spn-63673","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_legacy.export_canvas_graph_v1"},{"id":"spn-63674","text":" learn about routes on its own."}]},{"id":"blk-39976","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63675","text":"(b) The loss refusal reports "},{"id":"spn-63676","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"}]},{"id":"blk-39977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63677","marks":["code"],"text":"REPLACE_STATUS"},{"id":"spn-63678","text":" has four frozen terminal values. "},{"id":"spn-63679","marks":["code"],"text":"syntax_error"},{"id":"spn-63680","text":" is the only one whose "},{"id":"spn-63681","marks":["bold"],"text":"behaviour"},{"id":"spn-63682","text":" is exactly this case (refused, draft untouched, nothing for the author to repair). It is an imperfect "},{"id":"spn-63683","marks":["italic"],"text":"name"},{"id":"spn-63684","text":"; the diagnostic carries the honest code "},{"id":"spn-63685","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_DRAFT_LOSSY_WORLD"},{"id":"spn-63686","text":". Inventing a fifth status is a change to a published contract, not a language decision — hence the deferral."}]},{"id":"blk-39978","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63687","text":"(c) Routes emit "},{"id":"spn-63688","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-63689","text":" the edges, not interleaved"}]},{"id":"blk-39979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63690","text":"Sorting a route into edge order would need one comparison key spanning two vocabularies, and the two orderings are canonical for different reasons: an edge's order is "},{"id":"spn-63691","marks":["bold"],"text":"presentational"},{"id":"spn-63692","text":", a route's order "},{"id":"spn-63693","marks":["bold"],"text":"IS its minted ADMIT `sequence`"},{"id":"spn-63694","text":" (Q4). Interleaving would make an identity-bearing order look like a formatting choice. A route-free world therefore emits "},{"id":"spn-63695","marks":["italic"],"text":"exactly"},{"id":"spn-63696","text":" the pre-Slice-B text — no separator, no empty section (proved by "},{"id":"spn-63697","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5d"},{"id":"spn-63698","text":", see §3)."}]},{"id":"blk-39980","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63699","text":"(d) "},{"id":"spn-63700","marks":["code"],"text":"check_world_compatibility"},{"id":"spn-63701","text":" composes binding + reservation into one door"}]},{"id":"blk-39981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63702","text":"Both halves stay callable by name, but production goes through the composed door, because the failure mode of two independent checks is that a call site grows one and not the other — and the forgotten half is whichever was added second. Today that is the reservation. "},{"id":"spn-63703","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8i"},{"id":"spn-63704","text":" and mutation "},{"id":"spn-63705","marks":["bold"],"text":"M16"},{"id":"spn-63706","text":" are the rows that hold this."}]},{"id":"blk-39982","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63707","text":"(e) The bootstrap DSL gets "},{"id":"spn-63708","marks":["bold"],"text":"no"},{"id":"spn-63709","text":" route directive"}]},{"id":"blk-39983","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63710","text":"It is a frozen migration bridge. Its "},{"id":"spn-63711","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63712","text":" rejection was corrected, though: it used to say "},{"id":"spn-63713","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"a transition class, not an IR v1 edge\""},{"id":"spn-63714","text":", which is now false twice over — a route "},{"id":"spn-63715","marks":["bold"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-63716","text":" an IR v1.1 construct, and it was never an edge (D8). It now points at the surface that does have one. "},{"id":"spn-63717","marks":["code"],"text":"!!"},{"id":"spn-63718","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-63719","marks":["code"],"text":"=="},{"id":"spn-63720","text":" keep the old message. This is the identical correction commit 1 made for "},{"id":"spn-63721","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-63722","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-39984","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63723","text":"3. What the mutation round found"}]},{"id":"blk-39985","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63724","text":"Three survivors on the first pass, all three real. Recorded because they are the useful part."}]},{"id":"blk-39986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63725","marks":["bold"],"text":"M9 — the route separator emitted unconditionally. SURVIVED with nothing red."},{"id":"spn-63726","text":" The most useful finding. Whitespace is non-semantic, so no identity moved and "},{"id":"spn-63727","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5"},{"id":"spn-63728","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63729","marks":["code"],"text":"Q5b"},{"id":"spn-63730","text":" stayed green. And the formatter is "},{"id":"spn-63731","marks":["code"],"text":"graph -> text"},{"id":"spn-63732","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-63733","marks":["code"],"text":"text -> text"},{"id":"spn-63734","text":", so the extra blank line is a "},{"id":"spn-63735","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed point"},{"id":"spn-63736","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-63737","marks":["code"],"text":"Q3b"},{"id":"spn-63738","text":" (idempotence) stayed green too; the prediction that it would catch this was simply wrong. Meanwhile the canonical "},{"id":"spn-63739","marks":["bold"],"text":"bytes"},{"id":"spn-63740","text":" of every route-free world in the tree had moved — the exact law "},{"id":"spn-63741","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format"},{"id":"spn-63742","text":"'s own comment claims (\"no blank separator, no empty section\") and which nothing checked. "},{"id":"spn-63743","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q5d` exists because of this line"},{"id":"spn-63744","text":", and states the law structurally (a route-free world's text ends at its last edge) rather than pinning a literal, which would fork the emitter."}]},{"id":"blk-39987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63745","marks":["bold"],"text":"M11 — `replace_world_source`'s guard removed. `Q9e` stayed green."},{"id":"spn-63746","text":" "},{"id":"spn-63747","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-63748","text":" claims \"the draft is UNTOUCHED\". True, but for the wrong reason: the route-free twin of that source "},{"id":"spn-63749","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-63750","text":" the draft's current world, so a missing guard falls through to the semantic-noop branch and leaves revision 0 with the right candidate. "},{"id":"spn-63751","marks":["code"],"text":"Q9e"},{"id":"spn-63752","text":" is structurally unable to tell "},{"id":"spn-63753","marks":["italic"],"text":"refused"},{"id":"spn-63754","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-63755","marks":["italic"],"text":"silently accepted as a no-op"},{"id":"spn-63756","text":". "},{"id":"spn-63757","marks":["bold"],"text":"`Q9h`/`Q9i`/`Q9j` were added"},{"id":"spn-63758","text":": a paste whose lost world is a "},{"id":"spn-63759","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-63760","text":" world (two mailboxes + a route), plus a vacuity check that the twin really does differ."}]},{"id":"blk-39988","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63761","marks":["bold"],"text":"M14 — the reservation widened to every world. Reported as \"Q8 raised\"."},{"id":"spn-63762","text":" Not a production defect but a reporting one: "},{"id":"spn-63763","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-63764","text":" raised, and "},{"id":"spn-63765","marks":["code"],"text":"section()"},{"id":"spn-63766","text":" renamed the failure after its neighbour — so a reservation made too "},{"id":"spn-63767","marks":["bold"],"text":"strong"},{"id":"spn-63768","text":" read as a reservation that was "},{"id":"spn-63769","marks":["bold"],"text":"broken"},{"id":"spn-63770","text":". "},{"id":"spn-63771","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8b"},{"id":"spn-63772","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-63773","marks":["code"],"text":"Q8c"},{"id":"spn-63774","text":" are callables now and keep their own names. (This is the same lesson as run47's \"many laws share one error code\": a row must be identifiable as itself when it fails.)"}]},{"id":"blk-39989","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63775","text":"Also worth recording: "},{"id":"spn-63776","marks":["bold"],"text":"M5"},{"id":"spn-63777","text":" (body arity forked onto "},{"id":"spn-63778","marks":["code"],"text":"_rotor_dots"},{"id":"spn-63779","text":") is caught only at section granularity, and "},{"id":"spn-63780","marks":["code"],"text":"Q1d"},{"id":"spn-63781","text":" cannot see it at all — the rotor message happens to contain the same "},{"id":"spn-63782","marks":["code"],"text":"\"must have 4 lanes\""},{"id":"spn-63783","text":" while saying "},{"id":"spn-63784","marks":["italic"],"text":"rotor"},{"id":"spn-63785","text":" about a "},{"id":"spn-63786","marks":["italic"],"text":"body"},{"id":"spn-63787","text":". That is exactly the drift "},{"id":"spn-63788","marks":["code"],"text":"_body_dots"},{"id":"spn-63789","text":"'s docstring refuses, and it is why the two 4s are not one constant."}]},{"id":"blk-39990","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-63790","text":"4. Not frozen"}]},{"id":"blk-39991","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63791","text":"A route can now be "},{"id":"spn-63792","marks":["bold"],"text":"written, canonicalized, sealed, formatted, and refused for every reason it should be"},{"id":"spn-63793","text":" — and it still does nothing at runtime. Commit 4 folds it. Freeze the Slice B line after Commit 4, then promote "},{"id":"spn-63794","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-63795","text":" to Grounded in "},{"id":"spn-63796","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-63797","text":" §14."}]},{"id":"blk-39992","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-63798","text":"Carried obligation into Commit 4: unify "},{"id":"spn-63799","marks":["code"],"text":"route_body_in_range"},{"id":"spn-63800","text":" into "},{"id":"spn-63801","marks":["code"],"text":"admit"},{"id":"spn-63802","text":" to remove the fork (the obligation is written into the function's docstring)."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera4hvasflcsec4dl6qegc3zsspugsksvzlyzacsr4h3qotogucjhpq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}